│ amplification tests, enzyme immunoassays (EIA), direct fluorescent antibody, nucleic acid hybridization, and         │
│ transformation tests. Rapid tests include solid‐phase EIA and solid‐phase optical immunoassay. POC tests can be      │
│ performed within 30 minutes without the need for expensive or sophisticated equipment. The principal advantage of    │
│ this technology is the immediate presentation of results with the subsequent possibility to start the treatment of   │
│ infected patients immediately.                                                                                       │
